    delphi:hasVerdict "resolvable-now" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.82"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Inbreeding depression and heterosis are directly measurable with many public pedigrees and experiments. Standard mixed models can resolve the broad directional claim while testing alternative hybrid mechanisms." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Model fertility and offspring viability against pedigree inbreeding coefficients and genetic distance of mates, including hybrid lineages across generations. Decline under close inbreeding and recovery after outcrossing support the claim." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Effects vary among taxa and genetic backgrounds.", "Hybrid decline can also reflect segregation and incompatibilities." ;
